## 14. Summary

LLM jailbreak attacks attempt to manipulate models into bypassing their
normal safety restrictions. Important jailbreak techniques include
direct instruction manipulation, role-playing, hypothetical framing,
obfuscation, multi-turn attacks, many-shot attacks, adversarial
suffixes, automated jailbreak generation, and indirect prompt injection.

For AI agents, the security impact can be greater because agents may
interact with external tools and information. Effective protection
therefore requires multiple defensive layers, including filtering,
instruction separation, least privilege, monitoring, human approval,
sandboxing, and adversarial testing.

For an **Agent Resilience** project, jailbreak security can be evaluated
by testing multiple attack categories, measuring metrics such as Attack
Success Rate, applying defensive controls, and comparing results before
and after those controls are introduced.
